 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2021-05-20",
   "text": "Don't Weaponize the IRS Act\n This bill codifies regulations promulgated by the Trump Administration exempting certain tax-exempt organizations from specified reporting requirements. Specifically the bill \n increases from $5,000 to $50,000 the gross receipts threshold used to determine the eligibility of tax-exempt organizations for the exemption from certain disclosure and reporting requirements;\n expands the definition of organization to include tax-exempt charitable organizations and organizations with no significant activities relating to lobbying, political activity, and the operation of a trade or business;\n exempts from disclosure the names and addresses of contributors to an organization in its annual informational return; and \n extends exemptions from reporting requirements to political action committees (i.e., 527 organizations)."
  }
 ],
